<body class="antarctica">
<div class="draft-banner">Early access · Reservations are now open</div>
<header><a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="bitcoin++">bitcoin<span>++</span></a><span class="edition">ANTARCTICA / COLD STORAGE EDITION</span><nav aria-label="Expedition"><a href="#journey">The journey</a><a href="#people">The unconference</a><a href="#berths">Your berth</a><a href="#parka">Sponsorships</a><a href="/dashboard">Your account ↗</a></nav></header>
<main>
<section class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Bring bitcoin to the farthest reaches of the <em>globe</em></h1><p class="hero-deck">Some say it's a boat accident<br>waiting to happen</p><a class="button" href="{{ .CheckoutURL }}">{{ if eq .RemainingBerths 0 }}Join the waitlist{{ else }}Reserve Your Spot{{ end }} <span>→</span></a><div class="hero-facts"><span>ANTARCTICA</span><span>{{ if and .Conf .Conf.DateDesc }}{{ .Conf.DateDesc }}{{ else }}January 24–February 5, 2028{{ end }}</span></div></div><figure><img src="/static/img/antarctica/leading.png" alt="Illustration of an expedition ship, explorers, and penguins among Antarctic ice beneath an orange sky" fetchpriority="high" width="1024" height="1024"><figcaption>Southward, together.</figcaption></figure><div class="hero-seal" aria-hidden="true">₿<small>COLD<br>STORAGE</small></div></section>
<section id="journey" class="journey section"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">01 / The journey</p><h2>A little further<br>from the familiar.</h2></div><div class="journey-body"><p class="lede">A <span class="wordmark brand-inline">bitcoin<span>++</span></span> conference with an expedition at its heart. A place for conversations that deserve more than a hallway.</p><p>Cold storage keeps bitcoin offline. We’re taking the conversation somewhere colder. Bring your curiosity for an expedition of shared exploration, technical discussion, and time together.</p><div class="expedition-facts"><span><strong>13 days</strong>January 24–February 5, 2028</span><span><strong>12 nights</strong>Ushuaia round trip</span><span><strong>7 days</strong>Antarctic Peninsula</span></div></div>
<div class="expedition-gallery">
<figure><img src="/static/img/antarctica/kayaking.webp" alt="Kayak facing Antarctic mountains across calm water" width="600" height="450" loading="lazy"><figcaption>A different perspective.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src="/static/img/antarctica/penguins.webp" alt="Gentoo penguins on a rocky shore" width="600" height="480" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Meet the locals.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src="/static/img/antarctica/hiking.webp" alt="Hiker crossing snow below mountain peaks" width="600" height="400" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Take the long way.</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<figure class="expedition-map" id="expedition-map" aria-labelledby="expedition-map-heading">
  <div class="expedition-map-art"><a href="/static/img/antarctica/expedition-map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open expedition route map at full size"><img src="/static/img/antarctica/expedition-map.svg" width="720" height="700" loading="lazy" alt="Round-trip route from Ushuaia across the Drake Passage to the western Antarctic Peninsula"></a></div>
  <figcaption><p class="eyebrow">The expedition map</p><h3 id="expedition-map-heading">From the end of the road<br>to the edge of the ice.</h3><p>Depart and return in <strong>Ushuaia, Argentina</strong>. Cross the Drake Passage to explore the Antarctic Peninsula’s western coast and nearby islands.</p><h4>Possible places to explore</h4><ul><li>Neko Harbour &amp; Paradise Bay</li><li>Neumayer Channel &amp; Wiencke Island</li><li>Port Lockroy</li><li>Lemaire Channel, Pléneau &amp; Petermann Islands</li><li>Errera Channel</li></ul><p class="expedition-note">The shaded area marks the general exploration region. This is an illustrative route; landings and the sailing track depend on weather, ice, and expedition decisions.</p><a class="text-link" href="/static/img/antarctica/expedition-map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View full-size map ↗</a><p class="expedition-credit">Map data: <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Natural Earth</a>. Route based on the expedition itinerary below.</p></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="expedition-route"><p class="eyebrow">Your passage south</p><h3>Thirteen days beyond the everyday.</h3><ol class="expedition-days">
<li><div><span>Day 1</span><time datetime="2028-01-24">January 24</time></div><div><h4>Depart Ushuaia</h4><p>Board in Argentina and sail into the Beagle Channel.</p></div></li>
<li><div><span>Days 2–3</span><span>January 25–26</span></div><div><h4>Cross the Drake Passage</h4><p>Head south across open water, watching for seabirds.</p></div></li>
<li><div><span>Days 4–10</span><span>January 27–February 2</span></div><div><h4>Explore the Antarctic Peninsula</h4><p>Possible stops include Neko Harbour, Paradise Bay, and the islands around the Lemaire Channel. Activities may include kayaking, camping, hiking, snowshoeing, mountaineering, Zodiac outings, and photography workshops.</p></div></li>
<li><div><span>Days 11–12</span><span>February 3–4</span></div><div><h4>Return across the Drake</h4><p>Two days at sea on the journey north.</p></div></li>
<li><div><span>Day 13</span><time datetime="2028-02-05">February 5</time></div><div><h4>Arrive in Ushuaia</h4><p>Disembark and continue your onward journey.</p></div></li>
</ol><p class="expedition-note">Example route mapped to our expedition dates. Weather, ice, and expedition decisions determine landings and activities. Attendee-led sessions will fit around the expedition.</p><p class="expedition-credit">Itinerary and photographs sourced from <a href="https://www.adventure-life.com/antarctica/cruises/16115/antarctica-basecamp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Adventure Life’s Antarctica Basecamp trip</a>.</p></div></section>
<section id="people" class="people section" aria-labelledby="unconference-heading">
<p class="eyebrow">02 / The unconference</p><h2 id="unconference-heading">The attendees<br>make the agenda.</h2>
<p class="lede">An unconference, run by attendees. Bring a project, a question, or something you want to teach. The people on board shape the talks, demos, and discussions.</p>
<div class="unconference-details">
<article><h3>A room to build.</h3><p>We’ll have Starlink and a private room for impromptu hackathons, presentations, and post-expedition working sessions. Bring your laptop and pick up a project together after a day exploring.</p></article>
<article><h3>Bring something to share.</h3><p>Give a technical talk, show a work in progress, start a discussion, or join someone else’s hack. Sessions take shape around the expedition and the interests of the group.</p></article>
</div>
{{ if .Speakers }}<h3>Meet some of the people joining us.</h3><div class="speaker-grid">{{ range .Speakers }}<a href="{{ speakerPublicPath . }}">{{ if .Photo }}<img src="{{ speakerPhoto .Photo }}" alt="">{{ end }}<h3>{{ .Name }}</h3><p>{{ .Company }}</p></a>{{ end }}</div>{{ end }}
</section>
<section id="berths" class="section berths"><div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Find your berth</p><h2>Make room<br>for an adventure.</h2><p>Prices in USD, per person. Review the booking terms for inclusions and exclusions.</p></div><div class="berth-grid">{{ range .Berths }}<article><span class="eyebrow">{{ .Name }}</span><h3>{{ .Price }}<small>USD / PERSON</small></h3><p>{{ .Description }}</p><div class="deposit"><span>20% reservation deposit</span><strong>{{ .Deposit }}</strong></div><a class="text-link" href="#payment-options" data-berth-select="{{ .ID }}">Explore payment options ↗</a></article>{{ end }}</div></section>
<section id="payment-options" class="payments section"><div><p class="eyebrow">04 / Plan your passage</p><h2>More than one<br>way south.</h2><label class="berth-picker">YOUR BERTH<select id="berth-choice">{{ range .Berths }}<option value="{{ .ID }}" data-price-cents="{{ .PriceCents }}" data-pay-in-full="{{ .PayInFull }}" data-pay-in-full-savings="{{ .PayInFullSavings }}" data-deposit="{{ .Deposit }}">{{ .Name }} — {{ .Price }}</option>{{ end }}</select></label></div><div class="payment-visuals">
  <figure class="payment-timeline">
    <figcaption><span class="eyebrow">Compare your commitments</span><h3>The payment plan, at a glance.</h3><p>Five payments. One fixed fare.</p></figcaption>
    <ol class="installment-chart" aria-label="Five payments of approximately twenty percent">
      <li><span class="timeline-share">20%</span><span class="timeline-date">Reserve<span>Your deposit</span></span><strong data-installment-amount>{{ (index .Berths 0).Deposit }}</strong></li>
      <li><span class="timeline-share">20%</span><span class="timeline-date">Jan 1<span>2027</span></span><strong data-installment-amount>{{ (index .Berths 0).Deposit }}</strong></li>
      <li><span class="timeline-share">20%</span><span class="timeline-date">Apr 1<span>2027</span></span><strong data-installment-amount>{{ (index .Berths 0).Deposit }}</strong></li>
      <li><span class="timeline-share">20%</span><span class="timeline-date">Jul 1<span>2027</span></span><strong data-installment-amount>{{ (index .Berths 0).Deposit }}</strong></li>
      <li><span class="timeline-share">20%</span><span class="timeline-date">Oct 1<span>2027</span></span><strong data-final-installment>{{ (index .Berths 0).FinalInstallment }}</strong></li>
    </ol>
  </figure>
</div><div class="payment-grid"><article><p class="eyebrow">The payment plan</p><h3>20% now.<br>The journey ahead.</h3><p>Secure your spot with a <strong id="deposit-amount">{{ (index .Berths 0).Deposit }}</strong> deposit at booking.</p><ol class="payment-dates"><li><span>On reservation</span><strong>20% deposit</strong></li><li><span>January 1, 2027</span><strong>20% · <span data-installment-amount>{{ (index .Berths 0).Deposit }}</span></strong></li><li><span>April 1, 2027</span><strong>20% · <span data-installment-amount>{{ (index .Berths 0).Deposit }}</span></strong></li><li><span>July 1, 2027</span><strong>20% · <span data-installment-amount>{{ (index .Berths 0).Deposit }}</span></strong></li><li><span>October 1, 2027</span><strong>20% · <span data-final-installment>{{ (index .Berths 0).FinalInstallment }}</span></strong></li></ol><p class="fine">Five payments of approximately 20%, including your reservation deposit. Any rounding difference is included in the final payment.</p></article><article class="pay-in-full"><p class="eyebrow">Pay in full · Save 5% with bitcoin</p><h3>One payment.<br>All set for adventure.</h3><p>Pay for your entire trip at signup <strong>with bitcoin to save 5%</strong> on your berth fare. Pay with bitcoin or card via Stripe.</p><dl class="full-payment-summary"><div><dt>Standard passage fare</dt><dd id="full-standard-price">{{ (index .Berths 0).Price }}</dd></div><div><dt>Bitcoin savings · 5%</dt><dd id="full-savings">{{ (index .Berths 0).PayInFullSavings }}</dd></div><div class="full-payment-total"><dt>Pay in full with bitcoin</dt><dd id="full-payment-amount">{{ (index .Berths 0).PayInFull }}</dd></div></dl><p class="fine">USD per person for the selected berth, due at signup. The 5% discount applies only to full payment in bitcoin at signup. Your fare is paid in full, with no scheduled installments. Review the booking terms before reserving.</p></article></div><div class="booking-note"><div class="booking-note-copy"><strong>Reservations are now open.</strong><span>Choose your berths and payment plan in checkout.</span></div><a class="button" href="{{ .CheckoutURL }}">Claim your spot <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
<section id="booking-terms" class="section booking-terms" aria-labelledby="booking-terms-heading">
  <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Before you book</p><h2 id="booking-terms-heading">Your passage.<br>The details.</h2><p>Review the booking terms and traveler requirements before reserving your passage.</p></div>
  <div class="booking-terms-grid">
    <article><h3>Your berth</h3><p>Fares are in USD, per person, for the January 24–February 5, 2028 expedition. Reserve spots for your group, then arrange them across cabin types. Request an M, F or co-ed roommate for an unfilled twin cabin; triple and quad cabins default to co-ed. We’ll try to match preferences, but cannot guarantee them.</p><p>A group booking covers the selected number of passengers. Choose your group’s cabin arrangements during checkout. Cabin numbers and deck locations are not guaranteed.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Your payment plan</h3><p>Choose five payments of 20%, or pay in full at signup. Only full payment in bitcoin qualifies for the 5% discount. Card payments are processed by Stripe. Installments use the standard fare.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="#payment-options">Review amounts and payment dates ↑</a></p></article>
    <article><h3>Changes &amp; cancellations</h3><p>Final payment is due October 1, 2027. Cancel before that date for a refund of passage payments received, less the initial non-refundable 20% deposit. No refunds starting October 1, 2027 (America/Chicago). Passenger substitutions are not permitted.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Before you confirm</h3><p>Review your berths, total fare, payment schedule, inclusions and exclusions, and booking and traveler requirements before agreeing.</p><p>Medical, evacuation and repatriation insurance is required and purchased separately. <a class="text-link" href="/expeditions/antarctica/terms">Review terms and traveler requirements ↗</a></p></article>
  </div>
</section>
<section id="parka" class="section parka-sponsorship" aria-labelledby="parka-heading">
  <div class="sponsorship-banner"><span>Sponsor the expedition</span><span>For brands &amp; organizations</span></div>
  <div class="sponsorship-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">05 / Parka sponsorships</p><h2 id="parka-heading">Dress the expedition.</h2></div><div><p class="lede">Take your place on the expedition.</p><p>Put your brand on the arms, front, or back of the expedition’s signature layer.</p><p>Each placement covers approximately 22 parkas. Tickets are separate.</p></div></div>
  <h3 class="sponsor-packages-heading">Sponsorship packages <span>USD / placement across all parkas</span></h3>
  <div class="sponsor-rates" aria-label="Parka sponsorship rates">
    <article><p class="eyebrow">01 / Upper arm</p><h3>$7,500 <small>per placement</small></h3><p>2 placements</p></article>
    <article><p class="eyebrow">02 / Middle arm</p><h3>$6,000 <small>per placement</small></h3><p>2 placements</p></article>
    <article><p class="eyebrow">03 / Lower arm</p><h3>$5,000 <small>per placement</small></h3><p>2 placements</p></article>
    <article><p class="eyebrow">04 / Left chest</p><h3>$12,500 <small>per placement</small></h3><p>1 placement</p></article>
    <article><p class="eyebrow">05 / Right front</p><h3>$10,000 <small>per placement</small></h3><p>2 placements</p></article>
    <article class="sponsor-rate-featured"><p class="eyebrow">06 / Large back</p><h3>$25,000 <small>per placement</small></h3><p>1 placement</p></article>
  </div>
  <div class="sponsor-benefits"><h3>Beyond the garment.</h3><p>Benefits include linked website acknowledgment, inclusion in a sponsor announcement and expedition recap, and an agreed selection of expedition photographs for promotional use. Photo permissions and final deliverables will be agreed with each sponsor.</p></div>
  <figure class="sponsor-deck"><a href="/static/img/antarctica/parka-sponsorship.png?v=dress-20261023" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="View the parka sponsorship deck at full size (opens in a new tab)"><img src="/static/img/antarctica/parka-sponsorship.png?v=dress-20261023" alt="Parka sponsorship diagram showing numbered front and back placements corresponding to the six packages above" width="2048" height="1152" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption>Select the image to view it at full size.</figcaption></figure>
  <div class="sponsor-actions"><a class="button" href="/static/downloads/antarctica/btcpp-arctic-expedition-sponsor.pdf?v=dress-20261023" download>Download sponsorship deck (PDF) <span>↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="mailto:sponsor@btcpp.dev">Ask about sponsorship ↗</a></div>
  <p class="sponsor-note">Placement concept only. Final details agreed with each sponsor.</p>
</section>
